  "notes": "Drawn from 737-800 HL8240 (2025-05-04, right side, colors) and 777-300ER HL8008 (2018-11-03, left side; that photo's colors are heavily processed, used for geometry only). Still worn by most of the fleet in late 2026 while the 2025 livery is applied at repaints (777-300ERs HL8008, HL8209, HL8275 already repainted by early 2026). Belly not seen squarely: the light gray is taken to wrap under. Title place differs by type (x 0.2 on the 737's right side, about 0.13 on the 777's left). Re-checked 2026-11-15 on the 777-300ER (the commonest type, HL8250 from the right): the title runs 0.132 to 0.337, and on the 777 the Hangul title sits under the cockpit on both sides (x 0.044, length 0.032); the 737's right side has it further aft, under the start of the title (x about 0.2).",
  "history": "Introduced 1984 with Korean Air's rename from Korean Air Lines; superseded by the 2025 livery (standard) from March 2025, still flying on most of the fleet.",
  "commonest": true
